Do you enjoy other people's misfortunes?
The idea that one should feel bad when someone suffers a loss or other form of misfortune is embedded in most people's sense of moral responsibility. Young children may scream with delight when they win a family board game, but this ignoble reaction usually becomes less and less acceptable in anyone over the age of 8 or 9. your opponents, but you know you have to hold back to express it openly.
