Clinical psychology is a branch within psychology that is responsible for studying all those aspects related to mental disorders and, in general, mental health. The clinical psychologist is responsible for carrying out a work of evaluation, diagnosis, prevention and treatment of people who have some type of mental or behavioral disorder or problem, aiming to find psychological balance and avoid any type of discomfort or suffering.
Un clinical psychologist is a mental health professional who treats people who have some type of psychological discomfort, being in charge of diagnosing some mental disorders and later solving them through psychological therapy.
Therapy for adults.
In short, clinical psychology is capable of treating different psychological symptoms such as mental disorders (feeling of fear, unfounded worries ...), somatic disorders (which can appear in a constant or acute way) and behavior disorders (irritability, disorders of the sleep…).
