The Couples Help Process In the first place, in supportive therapy for couples, we work to find the real problem that gives rise to the conflict, since in a large number of occasions the reason that originates the problem is accumulated and unresolved past conflicts.
Once they learn to communicate and the problem is detected, they will work using different resources that aim to correctly manage existing and future problems between the couple. Once the therapy is finished, it will be the couple who must decide whether or not to continue together once they have spoken and discussed their decision.
