Many people who struggle with anxiety become anxious simply because of the feeling of anxiety itself. If you have this form of anxiety, you probably worry a lot about why the anxiety is there, if it will ever go away, and what you should do about it.
Therefore, they tend to search online a lot for strategies to use against anxiety. The problem is that you try very hard to control something over which you have no direct control.
Anything you do to try to lessen your anxiety right now guarantees more anxiety in the future. What you resist persists, and that is the root of this problem.
Anxiety stops being a problem when you stop treating it like a problem.
If you already had the rhythm of anxiety, would you be looking for articles online about anxiety?
Would you be listening to podcasts or watching videos about anxiety? No.
If you've already been overcome by anxiety, would you be spending time analyzing what to do with anxiety?
Would you avoid activities you want to do because you are anxious? No.
When you try this and your brain says, “Are you crazy?” you just ignore it and go about your day.
