Self-effective style: focus your EA on the analysis of the demands of the situation, to find the most appropriate response. These people have a high opinion about their own efficacy, which leads them to seek all the information about the situation and to develop competent coping skills.
Confrontation: Direct actions directed towards the situation (eg expressing anger towards the cause of the problem, trying to get the person responsible to change his mind ...)
Self-control style: mobilization of resources focused on regulating one's own feelings and actions triggered by stress (try not to rush)
Acceptance of responsibility style: acknowledging your own responsibility in solving the problem (apologizing, criticizing yourself, acknowledging yourself as the cause of the problem)
Planning style: mobilization of EA to alter the stressful situation, which imply an analytical approach to it (establish an action plan and follow it, change something so that things improve)
