When we mention the wordself-deception we refer to the different episodes in which a person lies to himself, this being one of the great problems that many minds must face. This type of problem occurs in those cases in which an individual convinces himself of areality that is completely false, but that is done in an unconscious way.
The big difference between the two concepts is that the latter refers to a situation in which the person himself isaware that he is not telling the truth, while in the case of self-deception, what the person does is accept a reality that is not true but is not aware that it is false.
This type of self-deception occurs very frequently, and it is common for those who suffer from it. they lie to themselves to convince themselves that the decision they have made was the correct one.
The big problem is that although it is a good intention, if it is repeated excessively it can become counterproductive and negative. This can be translated as that everything that is functional, if its duration is excessive or is taken in large doses, the effect that is achieved is different from the one that is desired.
This does not apply only to material goods, but can also be applied to social groups and other types of situations. In these cases, people tend to value more those things that they consider to have more value just because of their price or time invested.
Its main psychological effect is that the person who resorts to it keeps striving to achieve a goal that, on many occasions, does not fit within their values and principles. In this case, the person usually ends up being aware of the situation and feeling disappointed.
One of the subtlest ways to deceive yourself is to lying to other people in order to convince yourself of something at the same time, making reality look distorted.
It is based on a mechanism by which by repeating the same lie on different occasions to other people, it makes the lie become reality for that individual, thus creating a false truth.
Through the self-deception of consolation, the ego and self-esteem are protected, making these people think that nothing that happens to them is their fault, if not that they are, in all cases, victims of the situation they live or go through.
Its psychological effect is to prevent facing those problems that can make a person feel bad, making them think that they are impossible to overcome.
