People with this type of anxiety tend to be hypervigilant to the feeling of anxiety. They are often trying to gauge and analyze their feelings for clues as to what triggers them and what calms them down.
The most important concept to know about anxiety is that avoiding anxiety in the short term increases anxiety in the long term.
There is nothing to worry about and nothing to find out about it. You have the opportunity to move on with your life and do whatever it is that you would do if the anxiety was completely gone.
So cut all that activity out of your life. If there was a magic bullet that corrected anxiety, you would have found it by now anyway.
Let it exist. Even give in to a panic attack and go on living like you've already won the battle, so there's nothing left to fight for.
The funny paradox of this approach is that when people really engage with it, that's how the experience of anxiety begins to soften. When you cling to the goal of reducing anxiety, relief is impossible.
Surely what you're doing right now isn't working, so it's worth at least trying something different.
Why is psychological therapy important?
If you are still not completely sure about the importance of taking psychological therapy, here are 9 reasons why you should go immediately.
You will feel much better
Go to a psychological clinic on timewill prevent the development of disorders.It must be taken into account that most of the time fears and concerns are transformed into stress, phobias and anxiety. In the long run, it could become a disorder that, if not treated in time, can trigger big problems.
