My book focuses on the fascinating microcomputer that is the brain of bees and on the question of how much intelligence can be packed into a tiny speck of nervous tissue. I make an attempt to take readers into the cabin of a bee, to see what the world is like from their point of view, and take this as a starting point for the psychological and philosophical exploration of the unique mind of bees.
