The predictive power of artificial intelligence (AI) machine learning is accelerating discoveries in the life sciences.
The research team developed a hierarchical Bayesian regression AI model called PyR0 that can provide scalable analyzes of the full set of public data sets of SARS-CoV-2 genomes. The Bayesian model predicts emerging viral lineages.
Through systematic retrospective testing, we found that the model would have provided early warning and assisted in VoC identification if routinely applied to SARS-CoV-2 samples, confirming its utility for public health and underscoring the value of rapidly sharing genomic data. .
The scientists divided the genetic samples into groups and then analyzed the fitness of each group. Specifically, the team created 3000 clusters from 1544 PANGO lineages and modeled the fitness of individual lineages across 1560 geographies.
According to the researchers, their algorithm can be applied to different viral phenotypes, as well as to any viral genomic dataset.
