In the midst of its long journey through the Delta Quadrant to return to earth (ETA seventy years from the start), the Voyager starship encounters a species called the Borg. These aliens assimilate other species to acquire their knowledge and work, injecting them with nanoprobes that take over their minds; later, they surgically replace the organic material with manufactured parts to give their victims superior powers.
Voyager and other Star Trek series with the Borg accurately depict various aspects of the psychology of trauma. For example, the captain of the Enterprise, Jean Luc Picard, is haunted by his assimilation period, and years later, in Picard, he has a flashback while walking through an abandoned Borg ship.
