It is time to reconsider our understanding of the sexual relationship between men and women.
It is the awareness that sex makes babies, called reproductive awareness, that makes sex different for us than it is for animals. Reproductive consciousness in humans, which we may have discovered about 100 years ago, is based on two things that humans can do that no other animal can:
The reason we can do this is that we can reason about unobservable events, all the processes that link insemination to the birth of a baby.
The crises created by the nullification of the federal right to abortion make it clear that we have to think of sex between men and women as an interpersonal act; not one that can be a separate act for two people who exchange sexual performance based on their own interest.
Because the evolutionary psychologist treats human sexuality like animal sexuality, male and female sexuality were placed in separate and distinct silos of sexual desire, sexual pursuit, sexual performance, and sexual pleasure. Social structures built around distinct male and female silos ended up reinforcing the idea that men are "driven," "need" (the psychological equivalent of animal instinct) for sex more than women.
We reject the idea that sexual pleasure is for men, while motherhood is the main sexual motive for women.
Men and women were now equal in their right to have sex for pleasure and for procreation. Now, we can imagine sex as an interaction between men and women who understand that sex gives us as much pleasure as babies.
Abortion is a partnership effort
As one man put it… “To be frank, the most I've ever had to do (on reproductive responsibility) is pick up a monthly supply of pills from the pharmacy on the way home, or just ask, once, at the start of a sexual relationship, if my future partner was protected”. 6 He goes on to admit that… “when it comes to pregnancy prevention, that has been my entire burden, and I have reaped the benefits of being carefree.
Partner sex is negotiated sex. Negotiating sex in a truly coupled sexual encounter is an exploration of what each of you wants each time you have sex.
Do you want sex to make a baby?
