If you are going to have an MRI on your working brain, you will be placed in a large tube with magnets that rotate around it creating a magnetic field. Those magnets cause hydrogen atoms in the blood supply to spin, and a computer translates different spin rates (different amounts of oxygen) into a color-coded image that indicates activity levels in the brain.
